{"name":"Caliente","hex":"#95594a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Caliente","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An unincorporated community in Kern County, California, United States.","A city in Lincoln County, Nevada, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Caliente"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caliente (Calle Ciega album)","blocks":[{"text":"Caliente is the debut album by Venezuelan group Calle Ciega released in 1998, and re-released on August 6, 2002."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/Calle_Ciega_Caliente_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliente_(Calle_Ciega_album)","wikidata":"Q5019899"},{"title":"Caliente (Vox Dei album)","blocks":[{"text":"Caliente is the name of the first album recorded by the Argentine rock band Vox Dei, issued in 1970, their only LP for \"Mandioca\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Vox_Dei_Caliente_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliente_(Vox_Dei_album)","wikidata":"Q5019907"},{"title":"Caliente (Inna song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Caliente\" is a song recorded by Romanian singer Inna for her third studio album, Party Never Ends (2013). It was released on 4 May 2012 through Roton. The track was written by the singer, while production was handled by Sebastian Barac, Radu Bolfea and Marcel Botezan. \"Caliente\" features lyrics in Spanish, marking Inna's first song in that language. It is a salsa and 90s dance music-influenced song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/InnaCaliente.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caliente_(Inna_song)","wikidata":"Q638517"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"Caliente":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https:/